THE TYPESETTING SUBSET FOR FIRST LIGHT, under the PDF goal (recorded 2026-11-07). Nothing is built now. It shapes the PDF stroke.
RULED by Tony, 2026-11-07:
    Text source. A field's text is its own string value. If the field holds a group, the text is that group's text, read by an explicit check in kant as *field. One level only: a group that holds another group refuses by name. getText is unchanged; today it returns the held group's tag.
    Overflow. Text that doesn't fit its box is clipped between words, with a warning naming the field. No flag is set; noRoom means only "the field doesn't fit its parent". A single word wider than the box is clipped at the box edge, with the same warning.
    Units. A bare number in a form is in points (1/72 inch).
    Typesetting (Tony, 2026-11-07): one style vocabulary for fields, paragraphs and runs. A field's style is its paragraphs' style until the text changes style. A style change in text ends at the end of its paragraph, never at a line end, and never crosses a paragraph. Whether a change can end earlier, inside a paragraph, is to be decided.
    Runs (Tony, 2026-11-07). A style change inside a paragraph is a bracketed run, {styleName: text}. It ends at its closing mark, or at the paragraph's end. Runs nest, each starting from its outer run's style. An unknown style name warns by name and prints the text plain. A literal brace is doubled.
    Insertions (Tony, 2026-11-07). {name} with no colon inserts a named field's text. A field whose action produces text fires on every pour, and its answer is inserted. Inserted actions must give the same answer for the same state, since a pour runs more than once. Counting across a layout belongs to typesetting's state, not to field actions. A missing name refuses by name. Files are reached through a field that reads them.
    Layout context (Tony, 2026-11-07). Typesetting state lives in one layout context per pass: a kant group built fresh when a layout starts, handed to every pour and to each inserted action as its argument, and thrown away at the pass's end. It holds the pour cursor, the break record, and the counters (page, page count, footnotes). It is never stored on the frames.
