  THE STYLE IN EFFECT (Tony, 2026-11-09, SEQ 584 R5):
    A field starts with a copy of its enclosing field's style.
    Its attributes are processed left to right, each changing the style in effect; every style attribute inherits this way, align included.
    By convention style:= comes first on the line, so later attributes override it; a style out of place is the author's mistake.
    Drawing happens after every attribute is processed: fill, then borders, then text.
    What is built (a lookup: own, style, enclosing) gives the same answers wherever the convention holds, so no code changes for it now.
  Naming (Tony, 2026-11-09, SEQ 582 R5): form attributes are camelCase, no dashes, no capital last; the qualifier first and the thing last (topBorder, strokeColor, fillColor); a plain name (color, border) is the default case.
  Text (Tony, 2026-11-09, SEQ 582 R0-R3): a field takes font and color from its own attribute, else its style, else its enclosing field, walking up; resolved in kant, and displayText reads only the field it is handed. color falls back to black, and the font to Helvetica 12, when nothing up the chain names one (Tony, 2026-11-09, SEQ 583 R1). An attribute that names a field is spelled := (firstLight: fill:=, font:=). The inset is a fixed 4 points in the text floor.
